  "query_preview": "../Friday through Tuesday/... The ridge of high \npressure in the Gulf of Alaska looks to begin to break down into \nthe weekend. Overall, the weather pattern still looks fairly \nbenign, but there could be some convective showers forming in \nBritish Columbia with easterly flow aloft Saturday. Right now, \ninstability in the Alaska Panhandle looks quite low, so this \nshould limit chances of this activity approaching Southeast \nAlaska. \n\n With model discrepancies this far out, there is still uncertainty \nas to where the best chances for precipitation will set-up. Any \nprecipitation that does form looks to have fairly low accumulations \nfor the area (less than 0.5\").",
